#!/bin/bash
# project-work-trigger — once a night, after the projects job has planned: let
# Jori do the project tasks it may do on its own, and email the user what is
# ready for review (plugins/projects/jobs/project-work.md).
#
# launchd (ai.claude.project-work) fires this at a few times in the early
# morning; the first that finds tonight's projects run done (or that it is past
# the last chance) does the work, and the rest see the day is done and exit.
# Not cron: the run is a `claude -p` that needs the Max sign-in in the GUI
# keychain (lib/run-ephemeral-opus.sh).
#
# Spend is bounded twice: the lane's own weekly share (projects settings
# `work_weekly_share`, checked here against the fork cost ledger) and the
# allowance governor (bin/allowance-brake), which holds the run while the week
# is on pace to run out.

PLUGIN_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)"
KERNEL_TOOLS="$(cd "$PLUGIN_DIR/../.." && pwd)"
source "$KERNEL_TOOLS/agent/scripts/lib/script-job-env.sh"   # PATH, GOG_KEYRING_PASSWORD, JORI_INSTALL_TOOLS
SCRIPTS="$KERNEL_TOOLS/agent/scripts"
NODE="${JORI_NODE:-node}"
P="$PLUGIN_DIR/bin/projects"
DATA="$JORI_INSTALL_TOOLS/data/projects"
STATE="$DATA/work-state.json"
LOG="$JORI_INSTALL_TOOLS/agent/logs/project-work.log"
JOB_MD="$PLUGIN_DIR/jobs/project-work.md"
mkdir -p "$DATA/work-results" "$(dirname "$LOG")"
log() { echo "$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S') [project-work] $1" >> "$LOG"; }

TODAY="$("$NODE" -e 'process.stdout.write(require(process.argv[1]).today())' "$PLUGIN_DIR/lib/project-tasks.js")"
FORCE=0; [ "${1:-}" = "--force" ] && FORCE=1
LAST_CHANCE_HOUR="${PROJECT_WORK_LAST_HOUR:-8}"
HOUR="$(date +%H)"; HOUR=$((10#$HOUR))

done_today() { "$NODE" -e 'const fs=require("fs");const p=process.argv[1];let s={};try{s=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p,"utf8"))}catch{};s.last_date=process.argv[2];s.last_outcome=process.argv[3];s.at=new Date().toISOString();fs.writeFileSync(p,JSON.stringify(s,null,1)+"\n")' "$STATE" "$TODAY" "$1"; }

if [ "$FORCE" -eq 0 ]; then
  LAST="$("$NODE" -e 'try{process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(require("fs").readFileSync(process.argv[1],"utf8")).last_date||"")}catch{}' "$STATE")"
  [ "$LAST" = "$TODAY" ] && exit 0
  # Wait for tonight's planning pass, which picks and sizes the work; past the
  # last chance, work from what the ledger already holds.
  PLANNED="$(tail -n 1 "$JORI_INSTALL_TOOLS/data/projects-log.jsonl" 2>/dev/null | "$NODE" -e 'let s="";process.stdin.on("data",d=>s+=d).on("end",()=>{try{process.stdout.write(JSON.parse(s).date||"")}catch{}})')"
  if [ "$PLANNED" != "$TODAY" ] && [ "$HOUR" -lt "$LAST_CHANCE_HOUR" ]; then
    log "waiting: tonight's projects run is not logged yet"
    exit 0
  fi
fi

QUEUE_JSON="$("$NODE" "$P" task work-queue --json 2>>"$LOG")" || { log "work-queue failed"; exit 1; }
read -r OVER N PER_NIGHT LARGE <<<"$(printf '%s' "$QUEUE_JSON" | "$NODE" -e 'let s="";process.stdin.on("data",d=>s+=d).on("end",()=>{const j=JSON.parse(s);const pick=j.queue.slice(0,j.per_night||2);console.log([j.budget.over||j.budget.cap<=0?1:0,pick.length,j.per_night||2,pick.some(t=>t.size==="large")?1:0].join(" "))})')"
if [ "$OVER" = "1" ]; then log "skip: the lane's weekly share is used up ($(printf '%s' "$QUEUE_JSON" | "$NODE" -e 'let s="";process.stdin.on("data",d=>s+=d).on("end",()=>{const b=JSON.parse(s).budget;process.stdout.write(`${(b.share*100).toFixed(1)}% of ${(b.cap*100).toFixed(0)}%`)})'))"; done_today over-budget; exit 0; fi
if [ "${N:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then log "nothing Jori can work on tonight"; done_today empty; exit 0; fi

# The allowance governor, decided before the run (lib/allowance-gate.sh).
source "$KERNEL_TOOLS/agent/scripts/lib/allowance-gate.sh"
allowance_gate project-work "$TODAY"
if [ "$BRAKE_RC" -eq 3 ]; then
  log "held by the allowance governor: $BRAKE_REASON"
  # Past the last chance the night is over; the tasks wait for tomorrow.
  [ "$HOUR" -ge "$LAST_CHANCE_HOUR" ] && done_today held
  exit 0
fi
[ -f "$KERNEL_TOOLS/agent/config/models.env" ] && source "$KERNEL_TOOLS/agent/config/models.env"
# Sonnet at high for small and medium work; a large task gets Opus at xhigh. kernel-guard-ok: generic effort level names
RUN_ARGS=(--model "${JORI_MODEL_SONNET:-claude-sonnet-5-5}" --effort high)
[ "$LARGE" = "1" ] && RUN_ARGS=()
[ "$BRAKE_RC" -eq 4 ] && RUN_ARGS=(--model "$BRAKE_MODEL" ${BRAKE_EFFORT:+--effort "$BRAKE_EFFORT"})
export JORI_BRAKE_DECIDED=1

REPORT="$DATA/work-results/$TODAY.html"
POINTER="$DATA/work-results/$TODAY.pointer"
rm -f "$REPORT" "$POINTER"
log "start: $N task(s), large=$LARGE, ${RUN_ARGS[1]:-opus}"
TASK="Run the PROJECT WORK job for $TODAY. Take at most $PER_NIGHT task(s) from \`projects task work-queue --json\`, in its order.
Write the review email to $REPORT and its one-line phone pointer to $POINTER (Step 6)."
"$KERNEL_TOOLS/agent/scripts/lib/run-ephemeral-opus.sh" project-work "$JOB_MD" --task "$TASK" --timeout-min 90 ${RUN_ARGS[@]+"${RUN_ARGS[@]}"}
RC=$?
log "runner exit $RC"
done_today "ran:$RC"

# Anything left "working" was cut off: give it back to the queue's next night.
"$NODE" -e '
const pt=require(process.argv[1]);
pt.withLock((l)=>{for(const t of Object.values(l.tasks)) if(t.jori.state==="working"){t.jori.state="failed";t.jori.result={kind:null,link:null,summary:"The run ended before this task was finished.",failed:true,at:new Date().toISOString()};}});' "$PLUGIN_DIR/lib/project-tasks.js" 2>>"$LOG"

if [ -s "$REPORT" ]; then
  PTR=(); [ -s "$POINTER" ] && PTR=(--pointer "$(head -n 1 "$POINTER")")
  "$KERNEL_TOOLS/bin/digest-deliver" --subject "Chief of Staff: work ready for your review — $(date '+%a %b %-d')" \
    --body-file "$REPORT" --intent project-work --evidence-live "${PTR[@]}" >> "$LOG" 2>&1 \
    && log "review email sent" || log "review email failed (rc $?)"
else
  log "no report written"
fi
exit 0
